<title>GERMANY: German Jan-July metals data consolidate losses.</title>
<headline>German Jan-July metals data consolidate losses.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German metals processing in the first seven months of 1996 was weaker than in the same 1995 period, but year-on-year decreases slowed in July, according to official monthly data published on Monday.</p>
<p>Losses in semi-finished metals output over last year narrowed compared with Jan-June figures and castings figures also improved their performance versus first half results, data from statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) showed.</p>
<p>Primary metals output underwent a different scenario.</p>
<p>Output of primary aluminium, copper and zinc in Jan/July 1996 was above year-ago levels, but the lead over the same 1995 period narrowed compared with Jan/June 1996 figures.</p>
<p>Lead output in Jan/July extended its losses over 1995.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes -- METALS</p>
<p> OUTPUT		  July 96   Jan/July 96	 pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/July 95</p>
<p>primary aluminium    48,562     336,267		 +  1.7</p>
<p>electrolytic copper  51,294     344,566		 + 13.3</p>
<p>zinc		     28,106     191,210		 +  3.9</p>
<p>refined lead	   10,378     100,975		 - 27.4</p>
<p>SEMI-FINISHED METALS July 96   Jan/July 96	 pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/July 95</p>
<p>aluminium	     142,210     915,176		 -  5.9</p>
<p>copper		  129,486     837,892		 -  9.1</p>
<p>zinc		     16,897	96,196		 -  0.8</p>
<p>lead			4,261	25,851		 - 17.8</p>
<p>nickel		    1,427	10,371		 +  1.2</p>
<p>METALS CASTINGS	June 96   Jan/June 96	 pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/July 95</p>
<p>aluminium		36,972     283,813		 -  0.0</p>
<p>copper		    5,238	41,719		 - 17.9</p>
<p>zinc			5,326	37,527		 - 13.3</p>
<p>lead			  509	 3,815		 + 40.6</p>
<p>tin			    18	   123		 - 16.3</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures include alloys. Nickel castings data were not given.</p>
<p>-- Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
